    <string name="faq_updates_title">Installing and updating</string>
    <string name="faq_updates_body">Install the APK once. Later builds keep the same applicationId and sign with the same key, so Android upgrades AMS Keyboard in place instead of creating a second app. Settings, clipboard history and your enabled-keyboard state survive the update. If you ever see \"App not installed\" while updating, uninstall the old copy once: a debug APK and a release APK have different signatures and Android refuses to mix them.</string>
    <string name="faq_clipboard_title">Unlimited clipboard</string>
    <string name="faq_clipboard_body">Clipboard entries are stored without a length limit. The list only shortens the preview; pasting always inserts the complete text, in chunks small enough for Android\'s binder. \"Copy all\" grabs the entire field, even when it was never selected.</string>
    <string name="faq_copy_all_title">Ctrl + A, + C, + V, + X and Alt</string>
    <string name="faq_copy_all_body">Ctrl+A selects everything, Ctrl+C copies the selection, Ctrl+X cuts it and Ctrl+V pastes. Ctrl and Alt latch like real PC modifiers: tap Ctrl once, then tap A. Alt sends Alt-based shortcuts (Alt+A to Alt+Z) to the app, which is what many editing apps expect.</string>
    <string name="about_footer">AMS Keyboard · no ads, no tracking, no third-party branding</string>

